From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] pdfcraft-web: host bridge gets a read-only open, opened, requestSave, a save acknowledgement and canDownload/canPrint

docs/phase5/r6.md (owner 2026-11-08: xlsx, pptx and pdf edit through the document server). The host bridge gets what the
Docs bridge has (wordcraft 0127/0128): pdfcraft:open {readOnly, canDownload, canPrint} (an edit of a read-only document is
reverted at once, "{name} is read-only"; nothing is sent), pdfcraft:opened, pdfcraft:requestSave, pdfcraft:saved {ok} (the
document stays unsaved until the parent acknowledged every save; ok:false marks it unsaved again). The parent's document
replaces the one it opened before. canDownload:false refuses Save As and every browser download (ui-egui
HOST_WITHHOLDS_DOWNLOADS, "Not allowed"); canPrint:false closes the Print dialog. A shell around the app runs the bridge after
each frame's logic; DocId is public for it. The save stays pdfcraft's incremental update (the original bytes are a prefix).
---

diff --git a/apps/pdfcraft-web/src/main.rs b/apps/pdfcraft-web/src/main.rs
